usb: composite: keep the bind_fixup bcdUSB flag bit on GET_DESCRIPTOR

g_dnl_bind_fixup() raises bcdUSB to 0x0201 so Rockchip host tools classify
rockusb as a loader rather than a BootROM device (patch 0001). That value
does not survive: composite_setup() rewrites bcdUSB to a plain 0x0200 on
every GET_DESCRIPTOR(DEVICE), so the descriptor the host actually reads
always says maskrom and tools speak the 0x471/0x472 protocol this gadget
does not implement.

Preserve bit 0 instead of clearing it. Stating the USB revision is the
purpose of that assignment; discarding a flag the gadget deliberately set
is a side effect of it. Gadgets that never touch the bit are unaffected.
SuperSpeed keeps its unconditional 0x0310 — the loader convention is a
USB 2.0 one.

Upstream-Status: Pending (against v2026.07)
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
@@ -1051,7 +1051,16 @@
 				cdev->desc.bcdUSB = cpu_to_le16(0x0310);
 				cdev->desc.bMaxPacketSize0 = 9;
 			} else {
-				cdev->desc.bcdUSB = cpu_to_le16(0x0200);
+				/*
+				 * Preserve bit 0, which a gadget may have set
+				 * in bind_fixup: Rockchip host tools read it as
+				 * loader-vs-maskrom (0x0201 vs 0x0200). Stating
+				 * the USB revision must not clear a flag the
+				 * gadget deliberately raised.
+				 */
+				u16 flag = le16_to_cpu(cdev->desc.bcdUSB) & 1;
+
+				cdev->desc.bcdUSB = cpu_to_le16(0x0200 | flag);
 			}
 			value = min(w_length, (u16) sizeof cdev->desc);
 			memcpy(req->buf, &cdev->desc, value);
